# Phase 1 Version 3: Data-Aware Single-HGT Residual MoE

Version 3 preserves the validated Version 1 K=80 model as a frozen complete-history
backbone. Each sample contains one heterogeneous graph and executes HGT once. Five
causal selectors read post-HGT Event states and provide task-specific residuals.

## Data Flow

```text
one K=80 causal graph
        |
frozen V1 HGT, executed once
        |
full Event states + V1 full context
        |
five post-HGT structural readouts
        |
task-specific zero-initialized residuals
        |
uniform or task-conditioned Dense routing
        |
six frozen V1 prediction heads
```

The five selectors are Short Temporal, Team Sequence, Spatial, Actor Relation, and
Transition. Team Sequence is an explicit heuristic over team changes, not a ground
truth possession label. Sparse selections never create replacement graphs or
pseudo-`next` edges.

## Task-Aware Paths

Event type, time, position, acting side, acting player, and advantage retain the
Version 1 targets and loss weights. Residual output projections differ by task.
Downstream routers can observe detached predicted Event probabilities; Position and
Player can additionally observe detached predicted Side probabilities.

Two independent corrections are available:

* Position learns a zero-initialized correction toward the side-conditioned current
  endpoint transport rule.
* Player adds a zero-initialized candidate score residual based only on K=80 actor
  counts, recency, and last observed team relation.

Both paths exactly reproduce Version 1 before training.

## Experiment Stages

```text
E0        V1 equivalence
E1-S      homogeneous shared residual, uniform routing
E1-T      homogeneous task residual, uniform routing
E2        homogeneous task residual, Dense routing
E3        E2 plus Event/Side conditions
E4        structural readouts
E5-POS    best core plus Position correction
E5-PLAYER best core plus Player correction
E6        best core plus both corrections
```

Epoch 0 participates in selection. Event Macro-F1 is primary, subject to fixed
non-degradation limits for time, position, side, player Top-3, and advantage.

## Commands

Run tests:

```bash
OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=paper_1/Phase_1/src:paper_1/Phase_1/version_1/src:paper_1/Phase_1/version_3/src \
  paper_1/Phase_1/.venv/bin/python -m pytest paper_1/Phase_1/version_3/tests -q
```

Run one controlled stage:

```bash
paper_1/Phase_1/.venv/bin/python \
  paper_1/Phase_1/version_3/scripts/run_v3_experiment.py \
  --stage E4 --device cuda:0 \
  --output-root paper_1/Phase_1/version_3/experiments/controlled
```

Use `--validation-sampling all` for full validation. Version 1 and Version 2 files
are not modified by this implementation.

## Completed Results

All controlled stages used the requested England split, 48 training matches, 12
validation matches, 96 samples per match, 8 epochs, batch size 48, and seed
`20260715`. Initialization reproduces all six V1 outputs with maximum absolute
error below `1e-6`.

The Event-primary selection policy retained Epoch 0 for every stage. The controlled
V1 reference reached Event Macro-F1 `0.4465`; the strongest trained V3 result was
E6 at `0.4398`. Consequently, E0/V1 remains the selected final model.

The task-specific paths nevertheless produced clear diagnostic gains:

| Configuration | Event Macro-F1 peak | Position distance peak | Player Top-3 peak |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| E0 / V1 | 0.4465 | 37.84 | 0.1137 |
| E5-POS | 0.4326 | 22.98 | 0.1231 |
| E5-PLAYER | 0.4391 | 36.83 | 0.3346 |
| E6 | 0.4398 | 22.49 | 0.3477 |

These task peaks can occur at different epochs and are diagnostic values, not the
selected multi-task checkpoint. At E6's Event-best trained checkpoint, removing
the Spatial expert reduced Event Macro-F1 from `0.4398` to `0.4145`; removing Team
Sequence reduced Player Top-3 from `0.3477` to `0.3299`.

The selected E0 model was reevaluated on every event in all 12 validation matches
(`20,427` samples): Event Macro-F1 `0.4230`, Time MAE `1.8578` seconds, Position
distance `37.42`, Side accuracy `0.8326`, Player Top-3 `0.1221`, and Advantage
accuracy `0.7521`.

